Project Foo
═══════════

Project Foo provides a fast, reliable way to frobnicate widgets from the command
line. It is designed to feel familiar to anyone who has used less, grep, or
other classic Unix tools.

CI

Installation
────────────

Install from crates.io:

▏ cargo install foo

Or download a prebuilt binary from the releases page.

  From source

▏ git clone https://example.com/foo.git
▏ cd foo
▏ cargo build --release

Usage
─────

Basic invocation:

▏ foo input.txt --output result.txt

Common flags:

┌──────┬────────────────┐
│ Flag │ Description    │
├──────┼────────────────┤
│ -v   │ verbose output │
│ -q   │ quiet mode     │
│ -o   │ output file    │
└──────┴────────────────┘

▌ Note: Foo reads from stdin when no input file is given.

Configuration
─────────────

Foo looks for ~/.config/foo/config.toml. Example:

▏ verbose = false
▏ threads = 4

See the configuration reference for details.

